%erg v1
Title: Decouple test_check live-corpus test and guard shared fixture mutation
Created: 2026-05-05
Author: claude

--- log ---
2026-05-05T08:34Z claude created

--- body ---
Two related hygiene issues:

**1. Live-corpus test in `test_check.sh` at line ~207:**
```sh
$ERG check tickets/   # sanity: live repo must pass erg check
```
This test couples CI outcome to editorial decisions in `tickets/`. A legitimately
malformed ticket committed during development would fail CI without any clear
indication that the test suite itself is fine. Options:
- Add a `# sanity: live repo` label and document in test_check.sh that a
  failure here means a ticket is invalid, not a code bug.
- Move this assertion to a separate `make validate` target that is explicitly
  a lint step, not part of the unit test suite.

**2. Shared fixture mutation risk in `test_archive.sh`:**
The `$FIXTURES/0001-valid.erg` fixture is written once (line ~33) and reused
by "multiple file args pass" and "blocked-by sibling" tests later in the file
(comment at line ~32). Any future test inserted between creation and reuse that
mutates or removes the file will silently break the downstream assertions.

Fix: add an existence assertion immediately before each reuse site:
```sh
[ -f "$FIXTURES/0001-valid.erg" ] || fail "fixture 0001 unexpectedly missing"
```
Or copy the fixture inline at the point of reuse.
